$DIR/test.p:2:18: recover is not permitted in Plutonium (a panic cannot be stopped; return errors instead)
    In Plutonium, panic stops the program. A hosted program first runs the
    pending deferred calls, as Go does, but control never returns to the
    function that panicked, so there is nothing for recover to catch.
    Report failures that the caller can handle by returning an error instead.
    Resuming a function after a panic needs an unwinder, tables and runtime
    support that a kernel cannot rely on, and a panic in kernel code means the
    state is already wrong.
    Return an error instead:
        func parse(s string) (int, error) {
            if s == "" {
                return 0, errors.New("empty input")
            }
            ...
        }
    (see "Built-ins Plutonium does not have" in the Plutonium spec, section
    13.1)
    (run "pluto explain E2004" for a longer explanation)
